%S A400648 1,3,21,386,18490,2220897,642132309,432412702948,662020005194532,
%T A400648 2264748757964191955,17093221830661876534327,
%U A400648 281885950729594859601549246,10079330512695724741577686143054,776540028381473474156557332062154661
%N A400648 Number of equivalence classes under column permutations of (n+1) X n binary matrices having an n X n submatrix with permanent 1.
%C A400648 The rows are labeled; only columns may be permuted. Every qualifying matrix has distinct nonzero columns.
%C A400648 Equivalently, a(n) counts n-element families F of distinct nonempty subsets of {1,...,n+1} such that, for at least one element x, there is exactly one way to choose a representative from each member of F, with all representatives distinct and none equal to x.
%C A400648 Each family is counted once, even if several choices of x satisfy this condition.
%H A400648 Vaclav Kotesovec, <a href="/A400648/b400648.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..76</a>
%F A400648 a(0) = 1. For n >= 1, a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} (-1)^(k+1) * 2^(k*(n-k)) * (2^k * binomial(n+1,k) * a(n-k) - binomial(n+1,2) * binomial(n-1,k-1) * A003024(n-k)).
%F A400648 a(n) ~ c * n * n! * 2^(n*(n+1)/2) / A245654^n, where c = 0.6309598728724490029992... - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 06 2026
%e A400648 For n = 5, the family F = {{1,2,3,4,5,6}, {2,3,4,5,6}, {3,4,5,6}, {4,5,6}, {5,6}} is counted: excluding 6 forces the representatives, in reverse order, to be 5, 4, 3, 2, 1. Excluding 5 also gives a unique system, but F is counted only once.
%t A400648 a[n_] := a[n] = If[n < 1, 1, Sum[(-1)^(k+1) * 2^(k*(n-k))*(2^k*Binomial[n+1, k]*a[n-k] - Binomial[n+1, 2] * Binomial[n-1, k-1] * 2^((n-k)*(n-k-1)/2)*(n-k)! * SeriesCoefficient[1/Sum[(-1)^j*x^j/j!/2^(j*(j-1)/2), {j, 0, n-k}], {x, 0, n-k}]), {k, 1, n}]]; Table[a[n], {n, 0, 15}] (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 06 2026 *)
%Y A400648 Cf. A003024, A089482, A342598, A342599.
%Y A400648 Cf. A245654.
